# A BYTE PREFIX of run-with-dormancy.nq, cut at the sw:dormantCount terminator
# and at no other point. Every byte below is therefore still what
# prober/src/emit.rs's RunWriter wrote, and the cut is one a crash really makes:
# the dormancy section sits between the header's sw:emission terminator and the
# first chunk, so a sweep killed after publishing which endpoints it declined
# to ask and before probing the first one it kept leaves exactly this file.
#
# 12 quads, one run graph (urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-27T10:00:00Z), the same
# run IRI and the same instant as run-with-dormancy.nq, because it IS that
# file's first 12 quads. Never load the two together: they are one run.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXTURE IS FOR, and it is a defect that no other committed file can
# stage. The run carries sw:emission and no sw:finalised, so it is a run that
# did not finish, and it carries no sw:completedEndpoint at all, so it finished
# no endpoint. Loaded beside an older sweep that measured kadaster, every
# conjunct of EndpointMeasurements.newer_run_did_not_reach_this_endpoint holds
# for kadaster: there is a newer run, it is not kadaster's run, it promised to
# write incrementally, it never recorded finishing, and it never marked
# kadaster. So the endpoint page said "a later sweep did not finish and never
# recorded finishing this endpoint", which is a crash claim, about an endpoint
# that same sweep DELIBERATELY declined to ask and said so in the four quads
# below. Its dormancy declaration is complete: the section's own
# sw:dormantCount terminator is the last line of the file.
#
# A FINISHED declining sweep does not reach that sentence, because
# newest_finalised gates it, which is why run-with-dormancy.nq cannot stage
# this and why the defect survived stage 1c-b4's tests.
